WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.875
Data classification helps teams decide which controls are required for each kind of data.

2
00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:15.229
Practical categories may include public, internal, confidential, regulated, credential, customer, tenant, and security-sensitive data.

3
00:00:15.229 --> 00:00:18.631
The category does not need to be perfect to be useful.

4
00:00:18.631 --> 00:00:21.877
It needs to guide design decisions consistently.

5
00:00:21.877 --> 00:00:29.376
Data minimization means collecting, storing, copying, and displaying only what is needed for a specific purpose.

6
00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:34.865
If a feature only needs a customer reference, it may not need a full customer profile.

7
00:00:34.865 --> 00:00:41.822
If a log event only needs a correlation ID and a coarse outcome, it should not carry the full request payload.

8
00:00:41.822 --> 00:00:44.992
Data flow mapping makes sensitive data visible.

9
00:00:44.992 --> 00:00:55.196
It should identify where data enters the application, where it is transformed, where it is stored, where it leaves, and which systems or people can access it.

10
00:00:55.196 --> 00:01:05.864
A useful map includes clients, servers, databases, caches, queues, third-party services, logging systems, analytics systems, exports, and support workflows.

11
00:01:05.864 --> 00:01:08.260
Trust boundaries should be visible.

12
00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:19.006
Data crossing from browser to server, server to database, service to queue, application to log pipeline, or support tool to export file may need different controls.

13
00:01:19.006 --> 00:01:26.736
The boundary is where validation, authorization, redaction, encryption, and retention decisions become concrete.

14
00:01:26.736 --> 00:01:33.926
Avoid broad domain objects, DTOs, logs, exports, and telemetry events that carry more fields than necessary.

15
00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:44.053
A model built for internal business logic may contain fields that should never be returned to a client, copied to analytics, or included in a support ticket.

16
00:01:44.053 --> 00:01:51.010
Classification and minimization should happen early enough to shape those contracts before deployment.
